  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "e452a9f040e663e47ccfdf16f652d78fc0411990",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2370252388,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "This is fine by me.\n\nYou also mentioned adding a run-time check for requesting more bits than the width of the return type, that would be good (now or later).\n\nIn https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/19119 I added a check for the case where the length is a literal int, and only one dissector appeared to be blatantly using the wrong API.  I also added a check in the opposite direction (asked for fewer bits than the next size down), but this is a Note at best because there could be good reasons for wanting a wider type:\n- for convenience (e.g. calling a function that expects a certain width afterwards)\n- avoiding the risk of integer overflow (e.g. multiplying 2 uint8_t values together might get sliced rather than than promoted to unsigned int?)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
